A 6‑port industrial Ethernet switch is a compact networking device built for harsh factory floors; it typically provides four copper ports supporting 100 Mbps‑1 Gbps speeds plus two uplink ports that may be copper or fiber. Designed for operation from –40 °C to 75 °C, the unit offers EMI resistance, dust‑tight enclosures and vibration protection, enabling reliable data exchange among sensors, PLCs and edge controllers across automation lines, smart manufacturing cells, rail‑transit signaling, power‑grid monitoring and renewable‑energy installations.
